<div class="tab post-death" data-group="primary" data-tab="post-death">
	<section class="sheet-tab">

		{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert}}

		{{! No name heading here any more — the sheet header says what they are now, in place of
		    the playbook (see actor-header.hbs), so repeating it at the top of its own tab was the
		    same word twice on one screen. The Remove control stays: it is the only way to take an
		    insert back off, and edit mode is the only place it should ever be reachable from. }}
		{{#if stonetop.editMode}}
		<div class="stonetop-pdi-header">
			<button type="button" class="stonetop-pdi-remove stonetop-pdi-remove--danger">
				{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.removeInsert"}}
			</button>
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{! No description block and no "Finish/Review your … insert" button. The insert's own prose
		    said again what the lore sections below say in the form the player actually reads them
		    in, and the button's window asked questions this tab already displays the answers to.
		    The tab opens straight onto the insert's state.

		    `stonetop.postDeathChoices` survives in the context for its `notes` alone (below) —
		    the label, the count and the outstanding flag went with the button. }}

		{{! Lore sections: Terrible Purpose, Consequences, etc. `postDeathTab.lore` is the same list as
		    the tab should print it: in play, without the Thrall's Favor entry, which gets pips of its
		    own below. In edit mode its options carry the cautions and the GM's cross-off controls
		    (post-death-outcomes.js). }}
		<div data-pdi="lore">
			{{> "stonetop.lore-section" lore=(or stonetop.postDeathTab.lore stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.lore) editMode=stonetop.editMode}}
		</div>

		{{! What the fiction earned them, as buttons (post-death-outcomes.js). The triggers are the
		    table's to call; these only land the outcome. One button per outcome rather than per clause
		    of the Purpose, whose clauses pair them differently, and the hint says so. `aria-disabled`
		    rather than `disabled` on the ones with nothing to do, so the reason stays reachable by
		    keyboard and by hover; the handler ignores a press on one. }}
		{{#if stonetop.postDeathTab.outcomes}}
		<div class="details-section stonetop-pdi-outcomes">
			{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.postDeath.outcomes.title") collapse="postDeathOutcomes"}}
			<p class="stonetop-pdi-hint">{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.outcomes.hint"}}</p>
			{{#each stonetop.postDeathTab.outcomes.rows}}
			<div class="stonetop-pdi-outcome-row" role="group" aria-label="{{this.title}}">
				<p class="stonetop-pdi-outcome-title">{{this.title}}</p>
				<div class="stonetop-pdi-outcome-actions">
					{{#each actions}}
					<button type="button" class="stonetop-pdi-outcome-btn{{#if danger}} stonetop-pdi-outcome-btn--danger{{/if}}"
					        data-pdi-action="{{this.action}}" data-source="{{this.source}}"
					        {{#if disabled}}aria-disabled="true" data-tooltip="{{this.reason}}"{{/if}}>
						<i class="fas {{this.icon}}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
						<span>{{this.label}}</span>
					</button>
					{{/each}}
				</div>
			</div>
			{{/each}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{! The Thrall's Favor, as hold pips: a ticked pip is Favor HELD, and a click sets the track to
		    that pip. Its lore entry is left out of the list above in play, so the count is shown once. }}
		{{#if stonetop.postDeathTab.favor}}
		<div class="details-section stonetop-pdi-favor">
			{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.postDeath.outcomes.favorTitle") collapse="postDeathFavor"}}
			<div class="stonetop-pdi-favor-row{{#if stonetop.postDeathTab.favor.caution}} is-cautioned{{/if}}" role="group" aria-label="{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.outcomes.favorTitle"}}">
				{{#each stonetop.postDeathTab.favor.pips}}
				<button type="button" class="stonetop-pdi-favor-pip{{#if filled}} is-filled{{/if}}"
				        data-pdi-action="favor-pip" data-index="{{this.index}}"
				        aria-pressed="{{#if filled}}true{{else}}false{{/if}}" aria-label="{{this.label}}"
				        {{#unless @root.stonetop.postDeathTab.favor.canSet}}disabled{{/unless}}></button>
				{{/each}}
				<span class="stonetop-pdi-favor-count">{{stonetop.postDeathTab.favor.heldLabel}}</span>
				{{#if stonetop.postDeathTab.favor.caution}}<i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation stonetop-lore-option-caution" role="img" aria-label="{{stonetop.postDeathTab.favor.caution}}" data-tooltip="{{stonetop.postDeathTab.favor.caution}}" data-tooltip-direction="UP"></i>{{/if}}
			</div>
			{{#if stonetop.postDeathTab.favor.canSet}}
			<p class="stonetop-pdi-hint">{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.outcomes.favorHint"}}</p>
			{{/if}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{! The GM's "gain a Mark": Favor's overflow and Dark Succor. With none left to gain it resolves
		    as Unholy Vessel. Crossing one off is on the Mark itself, in edit mode. }}
		{{#if stonetop.postDeathTab.gainMark}}
		<div class="stonetop-pdi-gm-row">
			<button type="button" class="stonetop-pdi-outcome-btn" data-pdi-action="gain-mark">
				<i class="fas fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
				<span>{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.outcomes.gainMark"}}</span>
			</button>
			<p class="stonetop-pdi-hint">{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.outcomes.gainMarkHint"}}</p>
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{! What is written in rather than ticked: who the Terrible Purpose is about, what a
		    Revenant with STRANGE APPETITES eats. The lore section above prints WHICH option was
		    taken; none of these has a box on the printed insert, so without this they'd live only
		    inside the window that collected them.

		    Each row ASKS while `open` (edit mode, or an answer never given) and PRINTS once it
		    isn't — the same rule the Instinct below follows, and for the same reason: Death's Door's
		    chooser is reached once, on the roll that granted the insert, and the tab's own Choose
		    Your Fate buttons and a dropped insert Item never pass through it at all. }}
		{{#if stonetop.postDeathChoices.writeIns.length}}
		<div class="details-section stonetop-pdi-purpose">
			{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.postDeath.purpose") collapse="postDeathPurpose"}}
			{{#each stonetop.postDeathChoices.writeIns}}
			<div class="stonetop-pdi-writein-row">
				{{#if open}}
				{{#if picks.length}}
				{{! The option's own alternatives (STRANGE APPETITES' "Pick 1"), not free text — so
				    the tab offers the same closed list the chooser did rather than inviting a
				    sentence the healing trigger can't read. }}
				<span class="stonetop-pdi-writein-label">{{this.label}}</span>
				<div class="stonetop-pdi-writein-picks">
					{{#each picks}}
					<label class="stonetop-pdi-writein-pick-label{{#if (eq this ../value)}} is-chosen{{/if}}">
						<input type="radio" class="stonetop-pdi-writein-pick"
						       name="stonetop-pdi-sub-{{../option}}-{{../../stonetop.postDeathRadioGroup}}"
						       data-section="{{../section}}" data-option="{{../option}}"
						       value="{{this}}"{{#if (eq this ../value)}} checked{{/if}}>
						<span>{{this}}</span>
					</label>
					{{/each}}
				</div>
				{{else}}
				{{! One span around the label, not a bare text node: a flex label splits inline text
				    across its own tracks. }}
				<label class="stonetop-pdi-writein-field">
					<span class="stonetop-pdi-writein-label">{{this.label}}</span>
					<input type="text" class="stonetop-pdi-writein"
					       data-section="{{this.section}}" data-option="{{this.option}}"
					       value="{{this.value}}" placeholder="{{this.placeholder}}">
				</label>
				{{/if}}
				{{else}}
				<p class="stonetop-pdi-purpose-text"><strong>{{this.label}}</strong>: {{this.value}}</p>
				{{/if}}
			</div>
			{{/each}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{! Ghost: what you're bound to. Tethered reforms you beside it and its destruction is the
		    Final Consequence, so the move can't resolve honestly until it's named. }}
		{{#if (or stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.tether stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.needsTether)}}
		<div class="details-section stonetop-pdi-tether">
			{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.postDeath.tether") collapse="postDeathTether"}}
			<p class="stonetop-pdi-hint">{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.tetherHint"}}</p>
			<input type="text" class="stonetop-pdi-tether-input"
			       value="{{stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.tether}}"
			       placeholder="{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.tetherPlaceholder"}}">
			{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.needsTether}}
			<p class="stonetop-pdi-hint stonetop-pdi-warning">
				<i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation"></i>
				{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.tetherMissing"}}
			</p>
			{{/if}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{! Thrall: what Dark Succor took away for good, and what the master demands. Neither has
		    a box on the insert, so they get their own rows rather than being lost to chat. }}
		{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.crossedOffMarks.length}}
		<div class="details-section stonetop-pdi-crossed">
			{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.postDeath.crossedOff") collapse="postDeathCrossed"}}
			<p class="stonetop-pdi-hint">{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.crossedOffHint"}}</p>
			<ul class="stonetop-pdi-crossed-list">
				{{#each stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.crossedOffMarks}}
				<li><s>{{this.label}}</s></li>
				{{/each}}
			</ul>
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.masterTask}}
		<div class="details-section stonetop-pdi-task">
			{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.postDeath.masterTask") collapse="postDeathTask"}}
			<p class="stonetop-pdi-task-text">{{stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.masterTask}}</p>
			<p class="stonetop-pdi-hint">{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.masterTaskHint"}}</p>
			{{#if stonetop.postDeathTab.taskComplete}}
			<button type="button" class="stonetop-pdi-outcome-btn" data-pdi-action="task-complete">
				<i class="fas fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i>
				<span>{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.outcomes.taskComplete"}}</span>
			</button>
			{{/if}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{! The moves the insert brought with it. Rendered through the SAME move-group partial the
		    Moves tab uses for playbook moves, off the same `postDeathGroup` — so these are the
		    real owned Items, with their dice, their resource tracks and their drag-to-hotbar,
		    and they look and behave exactly like every other move on the sheet rather than like
		    a printed copy of one. Its own fold id: this group also renders on the Moves tab, and
		    one flat per-actor set holds both, so a shared id would fold them together. }}
		{{#if stonetop.movelist.postDeathGroup.moves.length}}
		{{> "stonetop.move-group"
		    title=(localize "stonetop.postDeath.moves")
		    note=null
		    collapseId="postDeathTabMoves"
		    moves=stonetop.movelist.postDeathGroup.moves}}
		{{/if}}

		{{! Instinct. Prints as the QUESTION — three options and their "(Choose 1)" — while it's
		    still open, and as the ANSWER once it isn't; `postDeathInstinctOpen` decides which, and
		    the sheet builds it (see StonetopCharacterSheet). Open means edit mode, or an Instinct
		    that has never been answered: that second case is live in ordinary play because
		    otherwise a character whose Death's Door happened away from the sheet has no way to
		    their own Instinct at all. Changing an existing answer is still an edit, matching the
		    playbook Instinct on the Details tab.

		    The radio `name` is suffixed per character. Grouping is document-global and these now
		    render in ordinary play, so two undead PCs' sheets open at once would otherwise share one
		    group and a click on either would clear the other's answer. }}
		{{#if stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.instinct.options.length}}
		<div class="details-section">
			{{> "stonetop.section-heading"
			    title=(localize "stonetop.postDeath.instinct")
			    collapse="postDeathInstinct"
			    note=stonetop.postDeathInstinctNote}}
			{{#if stonetop.postDeathInstinctOpen}}
			<div class="stonetop-instinct-options">
				{{#each stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.instinct.options}}
				<label class="stonetop-item{{#if selected}} is-checked{{/if}}">
					<div class="stonetop-item-header">
						<input type="radio" class="stonetop-item-check stonetop-pdi-instinct"
						       name="stonetop-pdi-instinct-{{../stonetop.postDeathRadioGroup}}"
						       value="{{this.value}}"
						       {{#if selected}}checked{{/if}}>
						<strong class="stonetop-item-name">{{this.word}}</strong>
					</div>
					<div class="stonetop-item-description">{{this.description}}</div>
				</label>
				{{/each}}
			</div>
			{{else}}
			<p class="stonetop-instinct-readonly">{{stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeInsert.instinct.selected}}</p>
			{{/if}}
		</div>
		{{/if}}

		{{else}}

		{{! No active insert — choose one. Death's Door grants these itself on a 6-; this is the
		    manual route, for a table that resolved the move away from the sheet. }}
		<div class="details-section">
			{{> "stonetop.section-heading" title=(localize "stonetop.postDeath.chooseFate") collapse="postDeathFate"}}
			<p class="stonetop-pdi-hint">{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.chooseFateHint"}}</p>
			<div class="stonetop-pdi-available">
				{{#each stonetop.postDeathInsert.availableInserts}}
				<button type="button" class="stonetop-pdi-activate" data-slug="{{this.slug}}">
					{{#if img}}<img class="stonetop-pdi-activate-img" src="{{this.img}}" alt="">{{/if}}
					<span class="stonetop-pdi-activate-text">
						<span class="stonetop-pdi-activate-name">{{this.name}}</span>
						{{#if description}}<span class="stonetop-pdi-activate-blurb">{{{this.description}}}</span>{{/if}}
					</span>
				</button>
				{{/each}}
			</div>
		</div>

		{{! The way out of a tab about being dead on a living character's sheet: nothing but the
		    request flag is holding it open, so this says it isn't wanted. Not offered when a slug
		    IS set and merely unreadable (a pack that hasn't loaded) — that tab belongs to a real
		    insert and the picker above is the way back to it, not out of it. Nor when a fate is
		    actually owed (canHidePostDeathTab): the tab is then drawn by the character's own state,
		    which this button doesn't touch, so it would redraw itself the instant it was dismissed.
		    Taking any insert brings the tab back, so this can't strand a character who dies later. }}
		{{#unless stonetop.postDeathInsert.activeSlug}}
		{{#if stonetop.canHidePostDeathTab}}
		<div class="stonetop-pdi-footer">
			<button type="button" class="stonetop-pdi-hide-tab stonetop-pdi-remove--danger"
			        data-tooltip="{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.hideTabHint"}}">
				{{localize "stonetop.postDeath.hideTab"}}
			</button>
		</div>
		{{/if}}
		{{/unless}}

		{{/if}}

	</section>
</div>
